    "nearestExisting": "F16 supplies the separate freight/knight routes, B43 the rising cargo handoff, and F19 the echo that must keep a plate occupied while cargo and launch travel away. Here those are three elevations of one shaft: recovery supplies the shade needed at the original overlook, and the lower machine changes the traversability of that original address.",
    "novelty": "The player first sees the final gap and locked high gate, then solves their causes on two floors below. The only lantern has a physical continuous itinerary through the cargo duct, clasp, receiving well, launch carriage and final gallery. The return crosses above the outbound route rather than exiting into a separate room.",
    "designNotes": "64\u00d748 tiles, 3.34 normal screen areas. One room state, one echo and one lantern; no scripted checkpoints or event-count exit locks. The clasp makes cargo retrieval deliberate rather than requiring a narrow returning-freight rendezvous. The final swap works across eight consecutive timings. A slower stationary swap leaves the weight correctly but loses the useful carriage speed and cannot reach the upper receiving balcony.",
